## Phase 3: Service Health Check (Docker)

### Backend Health Check

```bash
# Run backend container with dependencies
docker run -d --name kotlip-backend-test \
  --env-file ./envs/backend.env \
  -e DB_HOST=host.docker.internal \
  -p 8000:8000 \
  kotlip-backend:latest \
  gunicorn config.wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --workers 4

# Wait for service to start (adjust sleep time as needed)
sleep 30

# Check health endpoint
curl http://localhost:8000/health/

# Cleanup
docker stop kotlip-backend-test
docker rm kotlip-backend-test
```

### AI Server Health Check

```bash
# Run AI server container with model weights mounted
docker run -d --name kotlip-ai-test \
  --env-file ./envs/ai.env \
  -v ./backend_and_ai/ai_model/models:/app/ai_model/models:ro \
  -p 8001:8001 \
  kotlip-ai:latest \
  uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001

# Wait for model loading (AI server needs more time)
sleep 120

# Check health endpoint
curl http://localhost:8001/health

# Cleanup
docker stop kotlip-ai-test
docker rm kotlip-ai-test
```

**Note**: AI server health check may take longer due to model loading. Align `start_period` in `docker-compose.yml` (default 120s) with actual warm-up time.

## Phase 4: docker-compose Integration

### Full Stack Build

```bash
# 1. Navigate to project root
cd /home/jik/projects/kotlip

# 2. Build all services (without starting)
docker-compose build

# 3. Verify all images created
docker-compose images

# 4. Start services
docker-compose up -d

# 5. Wait for all services to be healthy
docker-compose ps

# 6. Check service health endpoints
curl http://localhost:8080/__nginx_healthz
curl http://localhost:8080/health/
curl http://localhost:8080/ai/health
```

**Expected result**: All health checks return HTTP 200.

### Service Dependency Verification

```bash
# 1. Check service logs for errors
docker-compose logs backend | tail -50
docker-compose logs ai | tail -50

# 2. Verify service connectivity
docker-compose exec backend python -c "import requests; r = requests.get('http://ai:8001/health'); print(r.status_code)"
docker-compose exec ai python -c "import redis; r = redis.Redis(host='redis', port=6379, db=0); r.ping()"

# 3. Verify media server connectivity
docker-compose exec backend ls -la /app/media
docker-compose exec ai ls -la /shared/media
```

## Phase 5: Full System Health Check

### End-to-End Service Verification

```bash
# 1. Nginx health check
curl http://localhost:8080/__nginx_healthz

# 2. Backend health check (via Nginx)
curl http://localhost:8080/health/

# 3. AI server health check (via Nginx)
curl http://localhost:8080/ai/health

# 4. Direct AI server health check
curl http://localhost:8001/health

# 5. Verify service communication (Backend → AI Server)
docker-compose exec backend python manage.py shell -c "
from config.ai_client import get_ai_client
client = get_ai_client()
print('AI client initialized:', client.base_url)
"

# 6. Verify Redis connectivity
docker-compose exec backend python -c "
import redis
r = redis.Redis(host='redis', port=6379, db=0)
print('Redis ping:', r.ping())
"
```
